    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Carl Friedrich Gauss showed that any centered optical system, however many lenses and refracting surfaces it contains, can be fully characterized in the paraxial approximation by linear algebra rather than surface-by-surface trigonometry: every elementary optical element is a linear map on the ray state (y, \theta) -- height above the axis and angle to it --">

.. only:: html

  .. image:: /api/gallery/optics/ray_optics/images/thumb/sphx_glr_plot_abcd_system_matrix_thumb.png
