.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Charles Kao and George Hockham&#x27;s insight that glass fiber could in principle be purified to carry light over kilometers launched the fiber-optic communications industry. The graded-index (GRIN) fiber profile that followed guides light by continuously bending rays back toward the core axis, rather than by a single sharp core-cladding interface: for the standard quadratic radial index profile n(r) = n_0(1 - n_2 r^2/2), paraxial rays oscillate sinusoidally about the axis instead of walking off it. grin_medium builds the ABCD matrix of exactly this profile; chaining it through OpticalSystem and calling trace_ray reproduces the self-confining ray trajectory below, contrasted against the same ray walking away from the axis in a homogeneous medium.">

.. only:: html

  .. image:: /api/gallery/optics/ray_optics/images/thumb/sphx_glr_plot_grin_fiber_guiding_thumb.png
